  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatApp_6
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You\u2019re contacted by a patient advocacy group that has partnered
    with your trial\u2019s research team. Because of your lived experience, they
    invite you to join a patient advisory council where your input can help shape
    how complex research findings are communicated to future patients and the broader
    community.\r\n\r\nHow can patient participants make a difference in how study
    results are communicated to the public?\r"
  explanation: "Patients can play a powerful role in how study results are communicated
    by helping ensure the language is clear and adding personal context through lived
    experiences. And because patients often hold trusted roles in their families,
    communities, or advocacy networks, they can help share study results in ways
    that build trust and understanding. Together, these contributions strengthen
    how study results are communicated and help ensure they reach \u2014 and resonate
    with \u2014 the people who need them most."
  correctAnswer: All the above
  incorrectAnswer1: By ensuring study results are written in plain language and are
    easy to understand
  incorrectAnswer2: By sharing their lived experiences to add context and relevance
  incorrectAnswer3: By acting as trusted messengers, sharing results in ways that
    foster community trust and understanding
  questionRole: 
  questionType: 
  questionStage: 
